    {
      "id": "blurb",
      "type": "text",
      "position": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": -360
      },
      "size": {
        "width": 750,
        "height": 200
      },
      "zIndex": 200010,
      "style": {
        "fill": "#fefcbf",
        "fillOpacity": 90,
        "textAlign": "start",
        "fontSize": 13,
        "fontColor": "#744210"
      },
      "data": {
        "label": "Booking Session Manager: target-state AWS deployment\nA proposal for where Booking Session Manager (in development, per the domain diagram one level up) would run: a standard three-tier AWS deployment behind CloudFront, with nested boundaries (Region > VPC > subnet).\nTags at this level: only GDPR is re-declared, and only on the components that differ (the ALB and NAT Gateway only route traffic, No PII; the app tier, RDS and ElastiCache handle the same session data as the service above, Pseudonymized). NIS2, owning team, business domain and lifecycle state belong to the whole service and are not repeated here."
      }
    },
